message: "If you use this course or toolkit, please cite it as below."
title: "Autonomous Driving: AI Safety and Security — an open course"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Milin
    affiliation: "Hochschule Kempten – University of Applied Sciences"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/milinpatel07/Autonomous-Driving_AI-Safety-and-Security"
url: "https://milinpatel07.github.io/Autonomous-Driving_AI-Safety-and-Security/"
abstract: >-
  An open, runnable course on the safety and security of automated driving: perception, failure analysis,
  functional safety (ISO 26262), SOTIF (ISO 21448), cybersecurity (ISO/SAE 21434), AI safety (ISO/PAS 8800),
  runtime assurance, regulation and safety cases. 40 Jupyter notebooks, professional templates, interactive
  browser tools and the tested Python toolkit avsafety.
keywords:
  - autonomous driving
  - automated driving systems
  - functional safety
  - ISO 26262
  - SOTIF
  - ISO 21448
  - ISO/SAE 21434
  - ISO/PAS 8800
  - AI safety
  - uncertainty quantification
  - safety case
